  ],
  "notes": "USAGE:\n- {侘|わび}しい{生活|せいかつ} (dreary life)\n- {侘|わび}しい{気持|きも}ち (lonely feeling)\n- {侘|わび}しい{風景|ふうけい} (desolate scenery)\nConveys a poetic, wistful loneliness rather than simple isolation. Often evokes imagery of autumn or winter, empty spaces, or solitary living.\n\nCULTURAL NOTE:\nRelated to the aesthetic concept of {侘|わ}び (wabi) - finding beauty in simplicity and imperfection, though the adjective emphasizes the melancholy aspect more than the aesthetic appreciation.\n\nFORMS:\n- Adverb: {侘|わび}しく\n- Noun form: {侘|わび}しさ (loneliness, dreariness)",
